      "traceTextDiagram": "Agent Daemon Bootstrap Flow\n├── daemon.Run() entry \u003c-- 1a\n│   ├── Open storage (agents, mailbox, etc.) \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/daemon.go:39\n│   ├── Load agent record from store \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/daemon.go:95\n│   ├── Generate trace ID \u003c-- 1b\n│   ├── Build tools.Config with HookDispatcher \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/daemon.go:118\n│   ├── tools.NewRegistry() \u003c-- 1c\n│   │   └── Register all tools (fs, code, etc.) \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:209\n│   ├── createAgent() \u003c-- 1d\n│   │   ├── Create ReActAgent with LLM \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/daemon.go:324\n│   │   ├── agent.Initialize(llm, signature) \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/daemon.go:404\n│   │   └── Tool registration loop \u003c-- 1e\n│   │       └── dspyAgent.RegisterTool() \u003c-- 1f\n│   ├── Start heartbeat ticker \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/daemon.go:175\n│   └── Poll loop \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/daemon.go:226\n│       └── mailboxStore.Poll() \u003c-- 1g\n│           └── Process messages (handleAsk/Cmd) \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/daemon.go:280",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe agent daemon is a **long-running process** that runs autonomous AI agents powered by DSPy's ReActAgent framework. The problem: agents need to **receive work requests** via a durable message queue, **execute tasks** using LLM-driven tool calls, and **send back results** - all while supporting **hook-based interception** of tool calls for validation, mutation, and observability.\n\nThe daemon solves this by bootstrapping a complete agent runtime: opening persistent stores for messages and state, creating a tool registry with hook integration, initializing a DSPy agent with an LLM, registering all available tools, and entering a poll loop to process incoming messages.\n\n## Details\n\n### Bootstrap Sequence\n\nThe daemon starts at `daemon.Run()` [1a], which orchestrates the entire initialization:\n\n1. **Storage initialization**: Opens multiple SQLite-backed stores (agents, mailbox, tasks, blackboard) to persist agent state and messages\n2. **Agent record loading**: Retrieves the agent's configuration including role, policy, and allowed skills\n3. **Trace ID generation** [1b]: Creates a ULID for correlating all tool calls and trajectory events in this daemon session\n4. **Tool registry creation** [1c]: Instantiates `tools.NewRegistry()` with a config that includes the `HookDispatcher` - this is critical because it enables **PreToolUse and PostToolUse hooks** to intercept every tool call\n\n### Tool Registration\n\nThe registry automatically registers **filesystem tools** (read_file, list_dir), **code tools** (search, symbol_search), **edit tools** (apply_patch), and others. Each tool function is **wrapped with telemetry and hook dispatch** before being exposed to the LLM.\n\n### Agent Creation\n\n`createAgent()` [1d] builds the DSPy ReActAgent:\n- Creates a `react.NewReActAgent` with max iterations and timeout\n- Initializes it with an LLM (Gemini, OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) based on configuration\n- Builds a signature defining the agent's role and expected input/output format\n- **Registers all tools** from the registry [1e, 1f] by iterating through `registry.List()` and calling `dspyAgent.RegisterTool()` for each one\n\nThis registration step is what makes tools **available to the LLM** - the ReActAgent will include tool descriptions in its prompts and parse tool calls from LLM responses.\n\n### Message Processing Loop\n\nAfter initialization, the daemon enters a **poll loop** [1g] that:\n- Calls `mailboxStore.Poll()` to fetch messages with a lease timeout\n- Routes messages by type: `MessageTypeAsk` for questions, `MessageTypeCmd` for commands, `MessageTypeConsoleAsk` for interactive sessions\n- Invokes `dspyAgent.Execute()` which triggers the **ReAct loop**: the LLM thinks, calls tools (which trigger hooks), observes results, and repeats until it produces a final answer\n- Sends reply messages back through the mailbox\n\nThe **hook dispatcher** configured in the tool registry [1c] intercepts every tool call, allowing skills to validate paths, block dangerous operations, inject context, or record patterns for optimization."
    },
