      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Tool Registry Creation and Registration\n├── NewRegistry() constructor \u003c-- 2a\n│   ├── Initialize PathValidator \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:190\n│   ├── Create InMemoryToolRegistry \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:196\n│   └── Register tool categories\n│       ├── registerAgentTools() \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:209\n│       ├── registerFSTools() \u003c-- 2b\n│       │   └── Create fs.read_file tool \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/fs_tools.go:19\n│       │       ├── Define InputSchema \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/fs_tools.go:22\n│       │       └── wrapWithTelemetry() \u003c-- 2c\n│       │           └── Returns wrapped func \u003c-- 2d\n│       ├── registerCodeTools() \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:215\n│       ├── registerEditTools() \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:218\n│       ├── registerTestTools() \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:221\n│       └── registerMailTools() \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:227\n└── Wrapped Tool Execution Flow\n    ├── Tool invoked by DSPy agent\n    ├── dispatchPreToolUse() \u003c-- 2e\n    │   └── HookDispatcher.Dispatch() \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:404\n    ├── Execute tool fn(ctx, args) \u003c-- 2f\n    └── dispatchPostToolUse() \u003c-- 2g\n        └── HookDispatcher.Dispatch() \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:459",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe agent daemon needs to expose **filesystem, code search, and editing capabilities** to an LLM-driven agent (DSPy ReActAgent). However, these operations require **security validation, observability, and extensibility** through hooks. The tool registry solves this by wrapping each tool function with a **telemetry and hook dispatch layer** [2c] before registering it with the DSPy agent, enabling interception of every tool call for validation, mutation, and observation without modifying the core tool implementations.\n\n## Details\n\n### Registry Construction\n\nThe `NewRegistry` function [2a] creates a tool registry that:\n- Initializes a **PathValidator** to enforce workspace boundaries and prevent path traversal attacks\n- Creates an in-memory tool registry from dspy-go\n- Holds a reference to the **HookDispatcher** passed in via config for tool call interception\n\n### Tool Registration\n\nRegistration happens in phases [2b]:\n1. **registerFSTools** registers `fs.read_file` and `fs.list_dir` [2b]\n2. **registerCodeTools** registers `code.search` and `code.symbol_search`\n3. **registerEditTools** registers `edit.apply_patch` and `edit.apply_structured_diff`\n4. Additional categories: agent tools, test tools, mail tools, blackboard tools\n\nEach tool is created with `dstools.NewFuncTool` which takes a name, description, JSON schema, and the **wrapped function** [2c].\n\n### Tool Wrapping\n\nThe `wrapWithTelemetry` function [2c] returns a **closure** [2d] that intercepts every tool call:\n\n1. **PreToolUse Hook Dispatch** [2e]: Calls `HookDispatcher.Dispatch` with `EventPreToolUse`, allowing hooks to:\n   - Block the tool call entirely\n   - Mutate the tool arguments\n   - Inject context for the LLM\n\n2. **Tool Execution** [2f]: If approved, executes the actual tool implementation (e.g., `r.readFile`)\n\n3. **PostToolUse Hook Dispatch** [2g]: Calls `HookDispatcher.Dispatch` with `EventPostToolUse`, allowing hooks to:\n   - Observe the tool result\n   - Enqueue follow-up actions\n   - Record patterns for optimization\n\n4. **Telemetry Recording**: Records tool call metadata (name, args, duration, result) to the session's tool call history\n\n5. **Trajectory Capture**: Optionally writes tool events to the trajectory store for pattern learning\n\nThis architecture ensures **every tool call flows through the same validation and observation pipeline** without coupling the tool implementations to the hook system."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "title": "Hook Dispatcher Initialization and Configuration",
      "description": "Hook system setup - loads hooks.yaml config, creates dispatcher with registry, initializes skill runner with executor and resolver for hook execution",
      "locations": [
        {
