          "lineNumber": 319,
          "lineContent": "for _, tool := range toolsRegistry.List() {",
          "title": "Tool registration in runtime",
          "description": "Runtime also registers all tools from registry to agent"
        },
        {
          "id": "7f",
          "path": "internal/agent/daemon/handlers.go",
          "lineNumber": 135,
          "lineContent": "return mailboxStore.Send(ctx, replyMsg)",
          "title": "Reply sending",
          "description": "Sends reply message back to asker via mailbox store"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Agent Daemon Message Processing\n├── Poll Loop\n│   └── for _, msg := range messages \u003c-- 7a\n│       └── switch msg.Type \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/daemon.go:280\n│           ├── handleAsk() \u003c-- 7b\n│           │   ├── Build task prompt \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/handlers.go:30\n│           │   └── dspyAgent.Execute() \u003c-- 7c\n│           │       └── ReActAgent tool call loop\n│           │           └── Tool registry invokes\n│           │               └── wrapWithTelemetry() \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:287\n│           │                   ├── dispatchPreToolUse() \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:334\n│           │                   ├── tool.Execute() \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:363\n│           │                   └── dispatchPostToolUse() \u003c-- internal/agent/tools/tools.go:328\n│           └── handleCmd() \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/daemon.go:284\n│               └── dspyAgent.Execute() \u003c-- internal/agent/daemon/handlers.go:184\n└── mailboxStore.Send(replyMsg) \u003c-- 7f\n\nRuntime Spawn Path (Alternative)\n└── Runtime.Spawn() \u003c-- internal/agent/runtime/runtime.go:128\n    ├── toolsRegistry.List() \u003c-- 7e\n    │   └── agent.RegisterTool() \u003c-- internal/agent/runtime/runtime.go:320\n    └── runSession() \u003c-- internal/agent/runtime/runtime.go:227\n        └── session.Agent.Execute() \u003c-- 7d",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nFoxctl runs **autonomous AI agents** that need to execute tools (like reading files or searching code) in response to messages. The challenge: agents must be **sandboxed and observable** - every tool call needs hook interception for security policies, telemetry, and pattern learning. The daemon bootstrap solves this by creating a **DSPy ReActAgent** with a tool registry that wraps every tool with hook dispatch, then polls a mailbox for work.\n\n## Details\n\n### Daemon Startup\n\nThe daemon entry point [7a] **polls a mailbox store** for messages addressed to the agent. When a message arrives, it's routed by type - `ask` messages go to `handleAsk()` [7b], `cmd` messages to `handleCmd()`. Each handler extracts the payload and builds a task prompt.\n\n### Agent Execution\n\nBoth handlers invoke **`dspyAgent.Execute()`** [7c] with the task prompt. This is a DSPy ReActAgent that runs a **reasoning loop**: it calls the LLM, which may return tool calls, which get executed, results fed back to the LLM, repeat until the agent produces a final answer. The agent was initialized during daemon bootstrap [1d] and had all tools registered [1e, 1f].\n\n### Tool Call Interception\n\nEvery tool in the registry is **wrapped with `wrapWithTelemetry()`** [2c]. When the DSPy agent calls a tool, the wrapper:\n1. **Dispatches PreToolUse hooks** for validation - hooks can block or mutate the tool arguments [4b]\n2. **Executes the actual tool** if approved [4e]\n3. **Dispatches PostToolUse hooks** for observation and side effects [4f]\n\nThis wrapping happens at registry creation [1c], before tools are registered to the agent.\n\n### Hook Execution\n\nHooks are **skills** (compiled binaries) that receive JSON input on stdin and return decisions on stdout. The hook dispatcher [5a] matches hooks by event type and filters (tool name, path regex), then the skill runner [5d] resolves the skill binary and executes it [5e]. The skill's output is parsed [5f] to extract the decision (approve/block) and any actions.\n\n### Reply Flow\n\nAfter `dspyAgent.Execute()` completes, the handler extracts the result from the returned map and **sends a reply message** back through the mailbox [7f], completing the request-response cycle.\n\n### Alternative: Runtime Path\n\nThe runtime provides an alternative spawn mechanism [7d] where agents are created programmatically rather than via daemon. It follows the same pattern: create tool registry [7e], register tools to agent [7e], then execute. This is used for multi-agent hierarchies where one agent spawns subagents."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Maps the initialization of the agent daemon with DSPy ReActAgent, tool registry creation with hook-wrapped tools, and the complete flow from tool execution through hook dispatch to skill runner execution. Key integration points: [1c] daemon creates tool registry, [2b] tools wrapped with hook dispatch, [4b] PreToolUse hook intercepts tool calls, [5d] hooks execute as skills, [6c] skills run with proper environment.",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph Daemon[\"Daemon Bootstrap\"]\n        1a[\"1a: Run entry\"]\n        1b[\"1b: Trace ID generation\"]\n        1c[\"1c: Create registry\"]\n        1g[\"1g: Poll messages\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph ToolReg[\"Tool Registry \u0026 Wrapping\"]\n        2a[\"2a: NewRegistry\"]\n        2b[\"2b: Register FS tools\"]\n        2c[\"2c: Wrap tool function\"]\n        2d[\"2d: Wrapped function\"]\n        2e[\"2e: Dispatch PreToolUse\"]\n        2f[\"2f: Execute tool\"]\n        2g[\"2g: Dispatch PostToolUse\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph HookSetup[\"Hook System Setup\"]\n        3a[\"3a: Create dispatcher\"]\n        3b[\"3b: Dispatcher factory\"]\n        3c[\"3c: Hook registry\"]\n        3d[\"3d: Skill runner init\"]\n        3e[\"3e: Load config\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph ToolExec[\"Tool Execution Flow\"]\n        4a[\"4a: Tool call start\"]\n        4b[\"4b: PreToolUse dispatch\"]\n        4c[\"4c: Check blocking\"]\n        4d[\"4d: Mutate input\"]\n        4e[\"4e: Execute tool\"]\n        4f[\"4f: PostToolUse dispatch\"]\n        4g[\"4g: Capture trajectory\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph HookDisp[\"Hook Dispatch Pipeline\"]\n        5a[\"5a: Dispatch entry\"]\n        5b[\"5b: Match hooks\"]\n        5c[\"5c: Hook runner invoke\"]\n        5d[\"5d: Resolve skill\"]\n        5e[\"5e: Execute skill\"]\n        5f[\"5f: Parse output\"]\n        5g[\"5g: Merge outputs\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Runner[\"Skill Runner\"]\n        6a[\"6a: Executor entry\"]\n        6b[\"6b: Runner invocation\"]\n        6c[\"6c: Build environment\"]\n        6d[\"6d: Select runner\"]\n        6e[\"6e: Exec runner\"]\n        6f[\"6f: WASI runner\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph Agent[\"Agent Message Handling\"]\n        7a[\"7a: Message iteration\"]\n        7b[\"7b: Route ask message\"]\n        7c[\"7c: DSPy execution\"]\n        7e[\"7e: Register tools\"]\n        7f[\"7f: Send reply\"]\n    end\n    \n    1a --\u003e 1b\n    1b --\u003e 1c\n    1c --\u003e 1g\n    \n    1c --\u003e|receives dispatcher from| 3a\n    3a --\u003e 3b\n    3b --\u003e 3c\n    3c --\u003e 3d\n    3e -.-\u003e|loads config for| 3a\n    \n    1c --\u003e|creates| 2a\n    2a --\u003e 2b\n    2b --\u003e 2c\n    2c --\u003e 2d\n    \n    2d --\u003e 2e\n    2e --\u003e|calls| 5a\n    2d --\u003e 2f\n    2f --\u003e 2g\n    2g --\u003e|calls| 5a\n    \n    5a --\u003e 5b\n    5b --\u003e 5c\n    5c --\u003e 5d\n    5d --\u003e|resolves to| 6a\n    5c --\u003e 5e\n    5e --\u003e|invokes| 6a\n    5f --\u003e 5g\n    \n    6a --\u003e 6b\n    6b --\u003e 6c\n    6c --\u003e 6d\n    6d --\u003e 6e\n    6d --\u003e 6f\n    \n    1g --\u003e 7a\n    7a --\u003e 7b\n    7b --\u003e 7c\n    7c --\u003e|calls wrapped tools from| 2d\n    7c --\u003e|uses registry from| 1c\n    7e --\u003e|registers tools from| 2a\n    7f\n    \n    4a --\u003e 4b\n    4b --\u003e|dispatches to| 5a\n    4c --\u003e 4d\n    4d --\u003e 4e\n    4e --\u003e 4f\n    4f --\u003e|dispatches to| 5a\n    4g\n    \n    style Daemon fill:#eebefa\n    style ToolReg fill:#fcc2d7\n    style HookSetup fill:#d0bfff\n    style ToolExec fill:#b2f2bb\n    style HookDisp fill:#ffec99\n    style Runner fill:#ffd8a8\n    style Agent fill:#99e9f2"
}